# Snapchat Clone MVP – Implementation Checklist (Post-Template Setup)

Assumes project created with expo-firebase-starter and `.env` configured.

## Phase 0 – Finalize Dev Setup & Stability Foundation ✅
1. ✅ Open the project in Cursor and let it index the codebase.
2. ✅ Initialize a Git repo if not already done and make initial commit.
3. ⚠️  Clean up or rename any unused starter components (e.g. HomeScreen). [Kept for now as basic logout]
4. ✅ Ensure Firebase services are active: Auth, Firestore, Storage.
5. ✅ Verify `.env` file is complete with Firebase config.
6. ✅ Set up folder structure if not included: `components/`, `screens/`, `api/`, `firebase/`, `functions/`.
7. ✅ Add ESLint and Prettier if desired for formatting consistency.
8. ⚠️  Confirm Expo runs the project via `npx expo start` and opens in emulator or Expo Go. [Needs Xcode]

## Phase 1 – Authentication & User Profiles
9. Customize Signup/Login screens to match app brand.
10. Add Firestore user creation logic post-auth if missing.
11. Load user profile into Zustand store or continue using Context if preferred.
12. Build profile screen and allow editing of username and profile image.
13. Implement privacy settings UI (post visibility, DM permissions).

## Phase 2 – Friends & Social Graph
14. Create `FriendRequest` model and subcollection structure.
15. Build screens to search users and send friend requests.
16. Implement accept/reject request flow with Firestore updates.
17. Display mutual friends and status on profile views.
18. Create `FriendSuggestionsScreen` using shared friend logic.

## Phase 3 – Ephemeral Posts & Stories
19. Build or replace camera screen with Expo Camera if not already included.
20. Upload media to Firebase Storage and log metadata to Firestore.
21. Add post/story expiration (`expiresAt`) and one-time view flag (`deleteOnView`).
22. Track viewer UIDs and implement deletion logic on view.
23. Set up Cloud Function or cron job to delete expired posts/stories.

## Phase 4 – Direct Messaging with Ephemeral Media
24. Create or adapt `ChatRoomScreen` for DMs with friends only.
25. Allow sending text, image, and video messages with expiration.
26. Store `viewedBy[]`, `expiresAt`, and `deleteOnView` in each message.
27. Delete messages on view or expiry using a scheduled job or client check.
28. Create chat list view showing most recent DMs.
29. Implement offline queuing and resend logic for DMs.

## Phase 5 – Feed, Reactions, Notifications, and Moderation
30. Create `FeedScreen` for posts/stories from friends/friends-of-friends.
31. Filter feed content based on visibility and friend status.
32. Add emoji reactions to posts/stories using `Reaction` model.
33. Enable push notifications via Expo or FCM for DMs and friend activity.
34. Add mute, block, and report user functionality.
35. Reserve `metadata` fields (e.g. `embeddingId`) for future RAG features.